  - $daemon-lifecycle
  - '#gnomon-up'
  - '#dev-launch'
  - '#identity'
  - '#approval-broker'
  - '#gnomon-helper'
  - '#session-runner'
learnings:
  - SBPL signing-identifier on process-exec matches the caller not the target; team-identifier is unbound in sandbox-exec
  - A bare copy of the signed helper executable is SIGKILLed outside its bundle; the helper serve refuses under any sandbox (exit 3)
  - A JS SIGUSR1 listener suppresses the inspector on Node 26 but is removable so the guard reads execArgv only
  - The Edit/Write tools convert backslash-u escapes into raw characters; write such test strings through a placeholder
tags:
  - gnomon
  - security
